    {
      "id": "supply-chain-hardening-astral-uv-guide",
      "tech": "Supply-chain hardening (Astral/uv guide)",
      "href": "https://astral.sh/blog/securing-from-supply-chain-attacks",
      "cat": "Standards & practices",
      "cat_id": "standards-practices",
      "times": 1,
      "why": "Astral's checklist (hash-pin GitHub Actions to SHAs, hash-check binary downloads, Trusted Publishing via OIDC, zizmor CI linter, dependency cooldowns of ~3 days, locked CI tools, script lockfiles, no sdist builds) maps to your Rust repos: Cargo.lock checksums, `--locked` everywhere, SHA-pinned Actions + zizmor on dailydiff/blog etc., Renovate `minimumReleaseAge`/Dependabot cooldown for cargo, crates.io trusted publishing, `build.rs`/proc-macros as the build-time code-execution risk.",
      "sources": [
        {
