    {
      "id": "airbnb-skipper",
      "tech": "Airbnb Skipper",
      "href": "https://github.com/airbnb/skipper",
      "cat": "Infra & platforms",
      "cat_id": "infra-platforms",
      "times": 1,
      "why": "Airbnb's open-source embedded durable workflow engine for Java/Kotlin: workflows and actions as classes, with checkpoints and replay, retries, waitUntil timers, signals, and Saga compensation, as a library on the database you already have (MySQL and SQLite today; Postgres is only on the roadmap). Parked as explore-only. Not a drop-in for Neon; useful as a reference for a small Postgres-backed durable-step pattern (claim/lease + idempotency keys) in Axum/SQLx. Closest relative is DBOS Transact (Postgres); contrast with Temporal/Restate, which are separate orchestration services. Qian Li (DBOS co-founder) framed the comparison, so treat that as partly promotional.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Qian Li post (Nov 23)",
          "url": "https://x.com/qianl_cs/status/2125005132626858088"
        },
        {
          "label": "Repo",
          "url": "https://github.com/airbnb/skipper"
        },
        {
          "label": "Airbnb blog",
          "url": "https://airbnb.tech/open-source/skipper-airbnbs-embedded-workflow-engine-is-now-open-source/"
        }
      ],
